        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5cb2efd0-e427-5e4a-a667-4f04453e1c2e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: North American Aviation\n- People: James H. Kindelberger\n- Products: T-6 Texan, P-51 Mustang, B-25 Mitchell, F-86 Sabre, X-15, XB-70, Apollo Command and Service Module, Saturn V second stage, Space Shuttle orbiter, B-1 Lancer\n- Roles: aerospace manufacturer, trainer aircraft\n- Organizations: United States Army Air Forces, United States Navy, Royal Air Force, British Commonwealth\n- Events: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- James H. Kindelberger led North American Aviation from 1934 to 1960.\n- During World War II, the North American Aviation T-6 Texan trained pilots for the United States Army Air Forces, the United States Navy, the Royal Air Force, and other British Commonwealth air forces.\n- The North American Aviation T-6 Texan is an American single-engined advanced trainer aircraft, and it remained in use into the 1970s.\n- North American Aviation was a major American aerospace manufacturer.\n- North American Aviation produced the T-6 Texan trainer, the P-51 Mustang fighter, the B-25 Mitchell bomber, the F-86 Sabre jet fighter, the X-15 rocket plane, and the XB-70.\n- North American Aviation also produced the Apollo Command and Service Module, the second stage of the Saturn V rocket, the Space Shuttle orbiter, and the B-1 Lancer.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "42250b1d-ab60-5204-af2e-3633f01156d2",
        "text": "Page: North American Aviation. Sentence: North American Aviation (NAA) was a major American aerospace manufacturer, responsible for a number of historic aircraft, including the T-6 Texan trainer, the P-51 Mustang fighter, the B-25 Mitchell bomber, the F-86 Sabre jet fighter, the X-15 rocket plane, and the XB-70, as well as Apollo Command and Service Module, the second stage of the Saturn V rocket, the Space Shuttle orbiter and the B-1 Lancer.\nPage: North American T-6 Texan. Sentence: The North American Aviation T-6 Texan is an American single-engined advanced trainer aircraft used to train pilots of the United States Army Air Forces (USAAF), United States Navy, Royal Air Force, and other air forces of the British Commonwealth during World War II and into the 1970s.\nPage: James H. Kindelberger. Sentence: He led North American Aviation in 1934-1960.",
